// =============================================================================
// meta_atac_resources.config — resource override for the Guo meta-analysis ATAC run.
// Layered on top of nextflow.config via an extra `-c` so the shared config is
// untouched.
//
// WHY: MERGED_REPLICATE_BAM_TO_BIGWIG:BEDTOOLS_GENOMECOV OOM-killed (exit 137) on
// Guo_g183618_KO on 2026-07-21 after ~5 days. That step pools all replicates of a
// group, and Guo ATAC libraries are ultra-deep (300-378M read pairs/run), so the
// pooled bedGraph is huge (KO = 12 GB) and `bedtools sort` holds it entirely in
// RAM (~10x the file size). It is process_medium (32.GB * attempt), so its three
// attempts were 32/64/96 GB — all killed.
//
// Observed: 9.0 GB bedGraph (MycKO) succeeded at <=96 GB; 12 GB (KO) needed more.
// g183618_WT has 6 replicates (deepest, not yet run) -> its pooled bedGraph may
// reach ~15-20 GB -> ~200 GB+. Fixed 320 GB covers that with headroom and stays
// under the 400 GB executor cap. Fixed (not attempt-scaled) on purpose: scaling
// from 320 would exceed the cap on retry and hang the task unschedulable.
//
// Scoped to MERGED_REPLICATE only; the per-replicate MERGED_LIBRARY bigwig tracks
// are shallower and already succeeded, so they keep the default allocation.
// =============================================================================

process {
    withName: '.*:MERGED_REPLICATE_BAM_TO_BIGWIG:BEDTOOLS_GENOMECOV' {
        memory = 320.GB
        cpus   = 4
    }
}
